 Version compatibility options from Line AA.
 -------------------------------------------
 NAVER  = 2, Use SWMM4x geometric parameter weighting.
 NFASNH = 1 on AA line re. surface area weighting. See documentation.

 Control information for simulation
 ----------------------------------

 Integration cycles.................         120

 Length of integration step is......       60.00 seconds
 Simulation length..................        2.00 hours

 NEQUAL value for the SWMM 42 Option          60

 Use U.S. customary units for I/O...           0

 Printing starts in cycle...........           1

 Intermediate printout intervals of         100 cycles
 Intermediate printout intervals of.      100.00 minutes

 Summary printout intervals of......         100 cycles
 Summary printout time interval of..      100.00 minutes

 Hot start file parameter (JREDO)...           0

 Initial time (TZERO)...............       15.00 hours
 This is time displacement from JIN interface file starting date/time when
 interface file is used.
 This also describes starting hour in K3 line hydrograph input when K3
 lines are used.
 Initial date (default).............        19880101 (yr/mo/day)
 NOTE: Initial date from JIN interface file will be used, if accessed,
 unless IDATZ is negative.

 Iteration variables: ITMAX.........      10
                      SURTOL........  0.0025
                      Surjun........  0.0000
                      Node Tolerance  0.0000
                      Link Omega....  0.0000
                      Node Omega....  0.0000

 Default surface area of junctions....   12.57 square feet.

 ITERATIVE EXTRAN SOLUTION. (ISOL = 2).
 NEWTON-RAPHSON SURCHARGE ITERATION.

 Surcharge Computations Use Preissman Slot Method

 NORMAL FLOW OPTION WHEN THE FROUDE 
 # IS GREATER THAN 1.0 (KSUPER=1)...

 NJSW INPUT HYDROGRAPH JUNCTIONS....     0

 Printed output for the following    1 Junctions

              1

 Printed output for the following    2 Conduits

            101        105

 Water surface elevations will be plotted for the following     1 Junctions

             50

 Flow rate will be plotted for the following     2 Conduits

            101        105

     INTERMEDIATE HEADER LINES ARE PRINTED AS IN ORIGINAL PROGRAM
     IDS ARE WRITTEN AS IN ORIGINAL PROGRAM 

     CONDUIT LENGTHS ON C1 LINE MUST EQUAL IRREGULAR SECTION LENGTH ENTERED ON THE C3 OR X1 LINES (IWLEN = 0)
     JELEV = 0 (DEFAULT). STANDARD INPUTS ARE DEPTHS NOT ELEVATIONS

     JDOWN = 0 - Minimum of normal or critical depth will be used at free outfalls (I1).

     Characteristic depth for M2 and S2 water surface profiles will be computed as in previous versions of EXTRAN (IM2 = 0).

     SEDIMENT DEPTHS WILL NOT BE READ FROM C1 LINES

